.TH VERBISAGE 1 "September 2026" "Verbisage 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
verbisage \- query word dictionaries and spelling suggestions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B verbisage
.RI [ options ] " command " [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verbisage checks words, suggests corrections, queries dictionary entries and
predicts words. It can use a local backend or connect to the session D-Bus
daemon. The packaged configuration selects the D-Bus client and a read-only
English Patricia dictionary.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Check whether a word exists in the selected dictionary.
.TP
.B correct
Return spelling suggestions.
.TP
.B query
Find words matching prefix, suffix or length constraints.
.TP
.B predict
Suggest a next word from preceding context.
.TP
.B config-dump
Display the effective configuration.
.TP
.B word-add, ngram-bump
Request dictionary updates. The packaged system Patricia dictionary does not
support these operations.
.PP
Use
.B verbisage command --help
for command arguments and options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Read an explicit configuration file.
.TP
.BI --language " tag"
Select a language, such as en_US.
.TP
.BI --mode " mode"
Select standalone or dbus client operation.
.TP
.BI --backend " chain"
Select a backend chain for local operation.
.TP
.B --verbose
Write diagnostic details to standard error.
.TP
.B --help
Display all supported options.
.SH FILES
An existing configuration under an absolute XDG_CONFIG_HOME, or otherwise
~/.config/verbisage/config.toml, takes precedence over
/etc/verbisage/config.toml unless --config is supplied.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR verbisaged (1)
